## Count the teenagers
Teenagers are under 20. The stem 1 row has three ages: 18, 18 and 19.
P(\text{teenager}) &= \frac{3}{28}
ANSWER: \frac{3}{28}

## Count the thirties with an even age
The leaves 2, 4 and 4 on stem 3 are even: 32, 34, 34.
P(\text{thirties, even}) &= \frac{3}{28}
## Count the forties with an odd age
The leaves 1, 3, 3 and 9 on stem 4 are odd: 41, 43, 43, 49.
P(\text{forties, odd}) &= \frac{4}{28}
## Add, since the two groups cannot overlap
P(\text{either}) &= \frac{3}{28} + \frac{4}{28}
&= \frac{7}{28}
&= \frac{1}{4}
ANSWER: \frac{7}{28} = \frac{1}{4}

## Write the slope formula
Use $P(4, 2)$ as $(x_1, y_1)$ and $Q(8, 5)$ as $(x_2, y_2)$.
m &= \frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}
## Substitute the co-ordinates
m &= \frac{5 - 2}{8 - 4}
## Simplify
&= \frac{3}{4}
ANSWER: m = \frac{3}{4}

## Use the perpendicular slope rule
Perpendicular lines have slopes whose product is $-1$, so the perpendicular slope is the negative reciprocal.
m_{\perp} &= -\frac{1}{3/4}
&= -\frac{4}{3}
ANSWER: -\frac{4}{3}

## Find the side length RS
$RS$ is a side of the square, and the circle is inscribed in the square (it touches all four sides), so the diameter of the circle equals the side length $|RS|$.
|RS| &= \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
&= \sqrt{(4 + 4)^2 + (17 - 11)^2}
&= \sqrt{64 + 36}
&= \sqrt{100}
&= 10
## Halve the diameter
r &= \frac{1}{2}(10)
&= 5
ANSWER: 5 \text{ units}

## Set up an equation
The water that dropped is a cylinder of radius 5 cm whose volume equals the sphere, $36\pi$.
\pi r^2 h &= 36\pi
\pi (5)^2 h &= 36\pi
25\pi h &= 36\pi
## Solve for h
h &= \frac{36\pi}{25\pi}
&= \frac{36}{25}
&= 1.44
ANSWER: h = 1.44 \text{ cm}

## Choose the trig ratio
In triangle $PQR$ the right angle is at $Q$, $|PR| = 120$ is the hypotenuse and $|QR|$ is opposite the 30° angle.
\sin 30^\circ &= \frac{|QR|}{120}
|QR| &= 120\sin 30^\circ
&= 120 \times \frac{1}{2}
&= 60
ANSWER: |QR| = 60 \text{ km}

## Find the arc length (Mary)
The arc is $\frac{106}{360}$ of the circumference, with $r = 100$.
\text{Arc} &= 2\pi r \times \frac{\theta}{360}
&= 2\pi (100) \times \frac{106}{360}
&= \frac{530\pi}{9}
&\approx 185.0049
&\approx 185
## Subtract John's distance
John sails the straight line $|ST| = 160$.
\text{Difference} &= 185 - 160
&= 25
ANSWER: 25 \text{ km}

## Find the area of sector RST
\text{Area} &= \pi r^2 \times \frac{\theta}{360}
&= \pi (100)^2 \times \frac{106}{360}
&= \frac{26500\pi}{9}
&\approx 9250.245
## Divide by 25 km² per ship
\text{Ships} &= \frac{9250.245}{25}
&\approx 370.01
&\approx 370
ANSWER: 370 \text{ ships}
